		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4540&amp;p=33872#p33872"><![CDATA[
Hi Daniel,<br>I'm sorry for the trouble.<br>Honestly the first translation I thought is really "<strong class="text-strong">Sostituisci Tx DMR ID</strong>", but if I haven't understood it bad, in the CPS settings <strong class="text-strong">Tx DMR ID</strong> can override the <strong class="text-strong">"global" ID</strong> with another one for every single channel in case people have multiple DMR ID's and have specific reasons to use different DMR IDs on different channels instead of using the <strong class="text-strong">"global"</strong> one.<br>So the meaning of the translation "<strong class="text-strong">Ignora Tx DMR ID</strong>" must be understood as ignore the <strong class="text-strong">"global" Tx DMR ID</strong> by replacing it with a different one.<br>In italian language, another possible translation could be "<strong class="text-strong">Scavalca Tx DMR ID</strong>" which also gives the meaning of dismissal/deposition of the <strong class="text-strong">"global" Tx DMR ID</strong> in order to replace it with a new one.<br>Also "<strong class="text-strong">Sostituisci Tx DMR ID</strong>" that you propose, is correct, but in my opinion it could be understood like to change the pre -existing <strong class="text-strong">"global" Tx DMR ID</strong> by replacing it with another different <strong class="text-strong">Tx DMR ID</strong>, as if the RTX was given or operated by third parties, which is also a function available in the OpenGD77 firmware which can be invoked directly by the transceiver:<br><br><a href="https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_UserGuide/blob/master/OpenGD77_User_Guide.md#station-dmr-id-number-entry" class="postlink">https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_Us ... mber-entry</a><br><strong class="text-strong">Station DMR ID number entry<br><br>    In Contact selection mode, press SK2 + Hash (#) key, and an alternative DMR ID can be entered for the radio (for test purposes) to temporarily override your normal DMR ID number which was loaded from the codeplug.</strong><br><br>I believe that the translation "<strong class="text-strong">Ignora Tx DMR ID</strong>" can be fine, perhaps "<strong class="text-strong">Scavalca Tx DMR ID</strong>" even better and a bit less equivocal, but I believe that each of the two translations has a certain degree of uncertainty that doesn't allow to prefer one rather than the other.<br>The matter would be a little different if the function label was something similar to "<strong class="text-strong">Override global Tx DMR ID</strong>" or something like that, because a possible translation into Italian would be a lot less ambiguous.<br>This is what I can write about it, considering that I'm not a professional translator and even my English unfortunately is not "Oxford level".<br><br>Daniel, many thanks for the message and the commitment you are putting in the development of the OpenGD77 firmware!<br><br>73 best regards de Fabio IZ2EIB<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=244">IZ2EIB</a> — Sat Nov 02, 2024 1:22 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
